  "solution": [
    "Draw the perpendicular from \\(C\\) down to \\(\\overline{AB}\\), meeting it at \\(E\\). Then \\(AECD\\) is a rectangle, so \\(AE = 8\\) and \\(EB = 14 - 8 = 6\\).",
    "In right triangle \\(CEB\\): \\(CE = \\sqrt{10^{2} - 6^{2}} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\\). So the height of the figure is \\(8\\).",
    "Area \\(=\\) rectangle \\(8 \\cdot 8\\) plus triangle \\(\\frac{1}{2}(6)(8)\\) \\(= 64 + 24 = 88\\). (Or: trapezoid \\(\\frac{1}{2}(14 + 8)(8) = 88\\).)"
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "P=figure['points']\nassert P['B'][0]==14 and P['C'][0]==8 and P['C'][1]==P['D'][1]\nEB=14-8\nh=sqrt(10**2-EB**2)\nassert h==8==P['C'][1]\nans=Rational(1,2)*(14+8)*h\nassert ans==88\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans\n",
